# The run ledger is append-only, and two branches that each run an agent both
# append to its end. Git's union driver keeps both sides' lines instead of
# raising a conflict over an edit neither side made, which is exactly right for
# a file where a line is a fact and no line ever replaces another.
#
# `log_agent_run.py` is idempotent on (agent, run_at, target), so a row that
# genuinely appears on both sides collapses the next time it is written rather
# than surviving twice.
.claude/runs.tsv merge=union
